    },
    {
      "id": "xWPoNoP0dhzBXasA5B8Mr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 250.03413713492057,
      "y": 1155.3789941111106,
      "width": 924.359375,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b44",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1279568261,
      "version": 1402,
      "versionNonce": 223819717,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793888492851,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Wave = the group of blocks running on the GPU at once. Blocks per wave =\nblocks that fit on the SM x number of SMs.\n\nWaves = div_ceil(blocks launched, blocks per wave): a partly empty last wave still costs\na whole wave (the tail effect).\n\nLast wave 68% full: 13 full waves = 13 x 216 = 2,808 blocks; 2,955 - 2,808 = 147 blocks\nare left for the 14th filling, so 147 of the 216 slots get a block and 69 stay\nempty (147 / 216 = 68%). About a third of the card sits idle during the last wave: there\nare no more blocks to hand out, so it takes about as long as a full wave but does\n68% of the work.\n\nA block goes to one SM, whole, and only when that SM has room in all four pools. When a block\nfinishes, the SM takes the next one from the grid. \n\nAfter wave 1, the waves blur: block 217 lands as soon as ANY block finishes, not when\nall 216 do. \n\nThe wave count is a model; exact only when all blocks take the same time.\n\nBlocks never wait for each other (transparent scalability): the same launch runs\non any card; more SMs or more fit per SM = fewer waves.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Wave = the group of blocks running on the GPU at once. Blocks per wave =\nblocks that fit on the SM x number of SMs.\n\nWaves = div_ceil(blocks launched, blocks per wave): a partly empty last wave still costs\na whole wave (the tail effect).\n\nLast wave 68% full: 13 full waves = 13 x 216 = 2,808 blocks; 2,955 - 2,808 = 147 blocks\nare left for the 14th filling, so 147 of the 216 slots get a block and 69 stay\nempty (147 / 216 = 68%). About a third of the card sits idle during the last wave: there\nare no more blocks to hand out, so it takes about as long as a full wave but does\n68% of the work.\n\nA block goes to one SM, whole, and only when that SM has room in all four pools. When a block\nfinishes, the SM takes the next one from the grid. \n\nAfter wave 1, the waves blur: block 217 lands as soon as ANY block finishes, not when\nall 216 do. \n\nThe wave count is a model; exact only when all blocks take the same time.\n\nBlocks never wait for each other (transparent scalability): the same launch runs\non any card; more SMs or more fit per SM = fewer waves.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
  "appState": {
    "gridSize": 20,
    "gridStep": 5,
    "gridModeEnabled": false,
    "viewBackgroundColor": "#ffffff"
